        "original_id": "f9de97cd-5bed-51ac-99ca-26ff7eb781c5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Warroad, Minnesota; Northwest Angle; Angle Township; Lake of the Woods County; Angle Inlet, Minnesota; Penasse, Minnesota; Magnusens Island\n- Radio Stations: KKWQ-FM; KRWB (AM)\n- Companies: Border Broadcasting\n- Historical Sites: Fort Saint Charles\n\nFacts:\n- KKWQ-FM 92.5 is a small local radio station that broadcasts from Warroad, Minnesota, a border town.\n- The Northwest Angle is a part of northern Lake of the Woods County, Minnesota, and it is coextensive with Angle Township.\n- Locals refer to the Northwest Angle simply as the Angle.\n- Border Broadcasting owns and operates KRWB (AM) and its sister station KKWQ-FM.\n- Fort Saint Charles was located on Magnusens Island on the Northwest Angle of Minnesota.\n- Fort Saint Charles was 3.5 miles east of Angle Inlet, Minnesota, and one mile southwest of Penasse, Minnesota.\n- Penasse, Minnesota, is the most northerly point in Minnesota.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
