        "text": "Page: KKWQ-FM. Sentence: KKWQ-FM 92.5, is a small local radio station broadcasting from the border town of Warroad, Minnesota.\nPage: Northwest Angle. Sentence: The Northwest Angle, known simply as the Angle by locals, and coextensive with Angle Township, is a part of northern Lake of the Woods County, Minnesota.\nPage: KRWB (AM). Sentence: It's owned and operated by Border Broadcasting, along with sister station KKWQ-FM.\nPage: Fort Saint Charles. Sentence: It was located on Magnusens Island on the Northwest Angle of Minnesota, 3.5 miles east of Angle Inlet, Minnesota and one mile southwest of Penasse, Minnesota, the most northerly point in that state.",
